{
  "dom_id": "step-q109881",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-0.45 \\\\ 1.55\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is a stochastic vector. Indeed, \n\n- its entries are all nonnegative, and\n\n- the entries add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.5+0+0.5=1\n$$\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$ is *not* a stochastic vector since the entries do not add up to one:\n\n$$\n0+0=0\\ne 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$u$ only.\"",
